  "notes": [
    "All figures represent Gini of expenditure, not income or wealth inequality. National Gini is not an arithmetic mean of provincial Gini.",
    "Values 0–1; higher means more unequal expenditure distribution within the measured area. The Gini is not a welfare or purchasing-power index.",
    "Regional group summaries report the median, range and distribution of published province-level Gini, NOT official regional Gini. No region Gini is computed from provincial coefficients.",
    "Urban and rural coefficients use within-area samples; the combined coefficient can lie outside the urban-rural pair due to between-area inequality.",
    "DKI Jakarta rural Gini is not reported by BPS (null). A dash or missing observation never means zero.",
    "Comparisons across the new Papua provinces and their 2024 boundary changes require care; do not splice unadjusted pre-split historical series.",
    "National March 2025, September 2025 and March 2026 values cited in the BPS release. Province historical time series not provided in this snapshot.",
    "Values copied from official BPS table, in the table's province order. SLI geographic-region tags are editorial organization only.",
    "Official Gini values must not be transformed into political-security scoring, investment recommendations or fabricated causal forecasts."
